A||||19||hyhy4u||Stupid Stupid Me!..Can someone tell me what i broke????||||9||
Z||000000||hyhy4u||08-15-2001||10:37 AM||||OK..so behind a local hardware store theres a nice long road that me and a buddy always time our cars 0-60 at...well i make one run and it was pertty crappy and i decide to make another run but shift my auto manually. Ok no problem so i thought..done it before..well i started off..went from 1st to 2nd..but it turns out i missed second and popped it into drive and then when i went from what i thought was 2nd to drive it was really drive to neutral so in neutral i gunned it and redlined it and i see some white smoke come out in the distance..ok thats problem number one..now the really relaly stupid thing i did..for some strange reason when i was still going like 40-50 i just threw my car into park!!..what the hell was i thinking..so my car starts grrrrrrrrr...down the road like im dragging something so i stand on the brakes and stop....get out..well nothings dragging..get in the car..try to restart it and it just kindof starts up and dies..did it again and it starts up fine..well my trans seems to be fine..park holds..reverse and 1-3rd all go fine..but somethings just not right..my engine starts right up but it kindof has a little faint wierd smell to it and when i shut off the engine this white smoke like hovers around my tailpipes..what the heck did i break this time???||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-15-2001||10:46 AM||||If there is no knock heard when it tries to run, sounds like you blew the head gasket. Pull your plugs and inspect them for moisture (sniff for coolant), then do a compression check.||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||08-15-2001||10:47 AM||||Sounds like coolant is getting into the combustion chamber, ie failed heat gasket from over-reving, cracked block, cracked head, ??? See what other have to say. <P>Trans should be OK, there's a safety in there that ratchets if you accidently put it in park.||||reg||5
Z||000003||hyhy4u||08-15-2001||10:50 AM||||so your telling me theres nothing at all wrong with the trans??..by the way its not leaking anything so could a cracked block still be it??||||reg||1
Z||000004||hyhy4u||08-15-2001||10:52 AM||||also the engine seem to still run as good as it ever did..its a 2.8 V6..il pull one of the plugs..how do I do a compression check??||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||08-15-2001||11:16 AM||||Is the smell kind of a sickening sweet odor?<BR>If so, it's probably antifreeze. Would seem to go along with the white smoke.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||California Kid||08-15-2001||11:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hyhy4u:<BR><B>also the engine seem to still run as good as it ever did..its a 2.8 V6..il pull one of the plugs..how do I do a compression check??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If there's no coolant under the vehicle, you're probably OK, but only if you don't spell antifreeze in the passenger compartment. It may be safe to run it, but keep a very close eye on both the coolant level and the oil level in engine, a variance in either one means something in the engine may have failed.<P>To check the cyclinders, you have to remove each plug and smell it. You can get a compression checker at most auto parts stores and they come with instructions. Wouldn't do this unless you notice the engine is running a little weird or you continue to see white smoke at exhaust tips.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||08-15-2001||12:44 PM||||Something else to check. <BR>Do this with the engine cold. <BR>Feel one of the the coolant hoses (the one from the thermostat housing is probably the easiest) for "stiffness". How easy is it to squeeze?<BR>Start the engine.<BR>Feel the same hose over a period of a minute or so.<BR>If the cooling system is pressurized immediately, while the engine is still cold, then you probably have a leak between a cylinder and a water jacket. <BR>If you continue to run it like this, something will eventually blow out. I'm guessing the heater core. (Saw it happen on another car.) <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||hyhy4u||08-15-2001||01:23 PM||||Hey Raydar..<P>  I did that with a cold engine but i dont really understand..i squezed it before i started it and it was really flexable..and after i started it..it wasnt as flexable but still was a little..not to much change..now do i keep it running for a little while and it should be like not flexable at all or what??||||reg||1
Z||000009||fieronv||08-15-2001||04:11 PM||||Another thing to check is the the color of your oil (brown is bad) and if any water is present in your oil. This is a classic symptom of a blown head gasket.<P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ambush||08-15-2001||06:43 PM||||From 50 MPH to  Reverse then Park in less than a second? I'm just glad to hear that you are OK. In an Auto tranny when people do what you did, sometimes the tranny could get stuck in a higher gear like 3rd. that would make it stall a few times and things of that nature....the smoke I can't help you with.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||08-15-2001||09:05 PM||||About the hoses...<BR>The car that I had in mind (was not a Fiero, BTW) had a blown head gasket. As soon as you started it, the compression from the cylinder(s) would leak into the cooling system. You could almost see the hoses expand, as the system was pressurized by the engine. This happened before the engine even warmed up. Took just a few seconds. The guy that owned it tried to drive it that way and the pressure finally blew out the heater core. <BR>This was an aluminum-head engine (3.8 Ford Taurus) that had been severely overheated. Made for a hell of a leak in the gasket.)<P>If your exhaust has a "sweet" smell, and is blowing white smoke, you're probably "burning" antifreeze. No guarantees that it will pressurize the cooling system like I described. Just something else to look for.<P>I've never heard of a head gasked being blown by over-revving an engine. Usually some moving part will break, or valves will float. I believe that Fieros are supposed to have a rev limiter built in to the ECM, anyway.<P>Hope this helps at least a little.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000012||hyhy4u||08-15-2001||09:39 PM||||If it is burning antifreeze whats wrong with it...and how big of deal is it to then fix it??..Thanks for all you guys input il try to keep ya posted||||reg||1
Z||000013||fieronv||08-15-2001||09:54 PM||||If you are burning coolant then you ave a blown head gasket or cracked head or cracked block. If it's only a blown head gasket (4 cycl.) not to bad to replace (6 cycl.) worse but not as bad a cracked part. DO NOT drive this car any further or more damage can occur ($$$$$). If you can do the work yourself make sure that the heads are not warped before putting everything back together or just take it to a shop and expect to see it again in a week or two. My wife blew a head gasket in her car (not a fiero) and it took the shop a week to complete the job and $700. While they had the engine apart I had them change all belt (timing included). Your head gasket could of just let go and not becuase you threw the car into park at high speed. Keep us posted on what you find out.<BR>Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000014||JamesWM83||08-15-2001||11:30 PM||||Ya know... often times over revving leads to piston rings goin out. I dont' know if anyone has mentioned this yet. When oil burns it creates white smoke... if your compression check come out that you have low compression... I'd have the rings checked out... and if it's not the rings.. they can fix the head gasket while they're at it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. hope that helps. Lates<P>------------------<BR>~James<P>1986 Fiero GT! <BR>2.8 4 clicker. White face guages, blue backlighting, grey marlbe dash kit, IRM sie rocker scoops, fierostore.com 1/4 window scoop, V8 Archie Warber hood, rear added sway bar, silver mesh inserts in tail-lights, mesh inserts in turn lamp and grill, KYB shocks and struts, Eibach lowering springs, 300 watt amp, and 600 watt 12" sub, clarion pro audio 5x6" plates, Kenwood Xcelon 4x10's, clarion pro audio cd player, monster calbe wiring, rockford wiring, pheonix gold wiring, chrome ocelot exhaust tips||||reg||1
Z||000015||hyhy4u||08-16-2001||10:57 AM||||Update!<BR>-oil level seems to be good<BR>-antifreeze level is still a little iffy, lol..if it is buring any its not buring it very fast<BR>-performance is all there<BR>-but now the wierdest thing..i dont know what persuaded me to do this but i pulled out the thermostat and it looks like someone hit it with a hammer..first off the rubber seal is half off..and one of the long shafts that runs from the top to the actual thermostat is bent at about a 45 degree angle..im talking this thing it trashed! heck i tried to bend the other side and it was rather difficult!..so now what?? Im gonna go buy a new one and put it in today and see what happens..any other inputs??||||reg||1
Z||000016||roadwarrior||08-16-2001||03:19 PM||||something you might want to check as a LAST RESORT is a cracked cylindre liner if this is the problem plan on spending big bucks if you can't swap engines yourself, the grinding noise and staling can possibly be caused by the torque converter.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Raydar||08-16-2001||05:05 PM||||I'd just replace the thermostat and drive it.<BR>Keep an eye on the coolant level for a while. Also make sure that the oil looks like it's supposed to. If it's got water in it it will be kinda light brown and foamy looking. If you get water in the oil, stop driving it immediately. The water will cause it to eat up bearings.<BR>The clatter that you heard when you threw it in park was the parking pawl (big steel pin) skipping past the hole that it locks into when the car isn't moving. Makes a hell of a noise, but probably didn't hurt anything. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000018||johnt671||08-16-2001||07:08 PM||||I would be surprised if you don't need to replace the tranny soon.  I hope not. so good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000019||hyhy4u||08-17-2001||11:35 AM||||Hey Guys..<P> Thanks for all the Help!..It seems now everythings ok..it dosnt smoke..dosnt burn any oil or antifreeze..Everything seems just dandy. Of course i will keep a eye on it and make sure everything is ok..whoo!..this thing had me scared for a while! Thanks Guys!<P> -Jason  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
